<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="71509" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/MSE/404/71509.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2025" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025.xml">2025</calendarYear><term id="120251" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring.xml">Spring 2025</term><subject id="MSE" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/MSE.xml">Materials Science and Engineering</subject><course id="404" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/MSE/404.xml">Laboratory Studies in Materials Science and Engineering</course></parents><sectionNumber>NP1</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Novel Photovoltaics</sectionTitle><sectionDateRange>Meets 17-Mar-25 - 07-May-25.</sectionDateRange><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Students are introduced to emerging photovoltaic materials through hands-on experiments. Students fabricate and characterize solar cells made of materials such as organometal halide perovskites. Different methods to synthesize/deposit these materials and device architectures are examined. Students then critically examine advantages and challenges associated with integrating new materials into photovoltaics.</sectionText><partOfTerm>B</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2025-03-17Z</startDate><endDate>2025-05-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="B3 ">Laboratory</type><start>02:00 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MW     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>204</roomNumber><meetingDateRange>Meets 17-Mar-25 - 07-May-25.</meetingDateRange><buildingName>Ceramics Kiln House</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Shim" firstName="M">Shim, M</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>